,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:64bd9eae7550c46bae0aefd9666f0630ec9cb5b42a29054abd70e5ea106145cf","file":"preprints/The-sharp-factor-of-IID-threshold-for-the-free-Ising-model-on-regular-trees-September-26-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":38,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"be9c81244afbbfb48a41717cf97ca0f010d924c4d20dab472b7dbba268c0f970","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-sharp-factor-of-IID-threshold-for-the-free-Ising-model-on-regular-trees-September-26-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:64bd9eae7550c46bae0aefd9666f0630ec9cb5b42a29054abd70e5ea106145cf","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-sharp-factor-of-IID-threshold-for-the-free-Ising-model-on-regular-trees-September-26-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L38"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\\label{thm:sharp}\nFor every integer $d\\ge3$ and every $\\beta\\ge0$, the free zero-field\nIsing law $\\mu_{d,\\beta}$ is a factor of IID in the sense of\n\\eqref{eq:equivariance} if and only if\n\\[\n                         \\tanh\\beta\\le(d-1)^{-1/2}.\n\\]\nIn this range the factor can be chosen to commute with every\nautomorphism on every label input."}
